derivative at the point $(4,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(4,2)} & =2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{4}-4\\cdot {2}^{-2} \\\\  & =8-1 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb46f74-a6ac-51dd-9716-053467775795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381197} {:answer/id #uuid "7c752b1e-3494-58b3-91b3-bc63d9070f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381198} {:answer/id #uuid "ba33d251-da28-523a-a29f-e0b6420aeb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381199} {:answer/id #uuid "57c21eba-c639-589d-a590-6b2758f94e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381200} {:answer/id #uuid "437f7400-06af-5d12-8795-82aceaaa029f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba33d251-da28-523a-a29f-e0b6420aeb9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381199} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc66302-048f-5b61-a77f-e57947059d3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381196}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "85a0874e-f8e3-58ee-a763-3ef7eef71825" :question/math-academy-id "q-159600" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=2x\\sqrt{y}-4y\\sqrt{x},$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\sqrt{y}-4y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\sqrt{y})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4y\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-4y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{y}\\cdot (1)-4y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{y}-\\frac{2y}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,4)} & =2\\sqrt{4}-\\frac{2\\cdot 4}{\\sqrt{1}} \\\\  & =4-8 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381202 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcd07b7-50b4-5ed1-b9d3-2a201e5d7d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381204} {:answer/id #uuid "1def416a-9115-5f32-affa-b8039b5e3e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381205} {:answer/id #uuid "c69f5c3f-2861-5ba1-aeb3-abdd43e0cb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381206} {:answer/id #uuid "70a9f79d-b5dc-5ada-901e-3f661c7aa60d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381207} {:answer/id #uuid "1d3a15eb-a517-5392-b575-6d93c1835d8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c69f5c3f-2861-5ba1-aeb3-abdd43e0cb6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381206} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6cd008-5190-5b59-930e-c8142bae276f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381203}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b549b8fe-2ea6-52d5-aba5-f73f5834b6db" :question/math-academy-id "q-159601" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}$ at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)-x\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{y})-x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y}{|}_{(\\pi ,\\pi /2)} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}-\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0ef6ef-d5c2-5f7d-b007-5d1f8bcb76dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381211} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d3c50a-be40-5168-9b60-89cddf3610ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381212} {:answer/id #uuid "885ea363-dc99-5baa-bdb0-83b42d304c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381213} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4f7612-4c6b-5535-81d9-f5903c791c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381214} {:answer/id #uuid "f9925be6-c2b3-5b22-8f0f-b02e6fe00ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381215}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7e4f7612-4c6b-5535-81d9-f5903c791c1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381214} :answer-field/id #uuid "47162c79-8d31-5bc6-a2b7-3b78e065d6f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381210}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4e2a2cf2-39c7-5aaf-aba5-b368c09836a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-159606" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)={y}^{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-{x}^{2}{y}^{2},$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{3}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}{y}^{2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)-{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡x)-{y}^{2}\\cdot (2x) \\\\  & =-{y}^{3}{csc}^{2}⁡x-2x{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(\\frac{\\pi }{2},1) & =-(1)^{3}\\cdot {csc}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot 1-\\pi  \\\\  & =-1-\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a19112-03ca-50b8-84a1-fe692ba95087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436300} {:answer/id #uuid "60c0f614-7c90-5e8c-8d18-e07fc305806f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436301} {:answer/id #uuid "9e7a5161-9c2f-5c14-b85f-c8f0665e4971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436308} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ff159b-22e8-5203-b53e-81a9138124a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436311} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c6a17e-95c5-56f6-8ecd-f1ad41f668be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2ff159b-22e8-5203-b53e-81a9138124a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436311} :answer-field/id #uuid "db764a00-316f-56d9-8f40-2a0441db7ae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186436327}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "90392678-f725-5c12-933c-87fa3256c47c" :question/math-academy-id "q-159609" :question/problem "For the function $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y},$ evaluate ${f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3).$" :question/worked-solution "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{5}{e}^{y}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-2{e}^{y}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =y\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})-2{e}^{y}\\cdot (5{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{x}-10{x}^{4}{e}^{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{1}-10\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-10\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-30\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}]}
